@startuml InquiryUserProfile

title Inquiry User Profile API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Inquiry User Profile Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "m_user_information" as m_user_information
end box

user -> page: Read own profile
activate page
page -> api: GET v1/user/profile (Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp; no query/body)
activate api
api -> app: [**InquiryUserProfileQueryHandler**] Process request
activate app
    note over app, infra
        Execution order: validate empty query/body and timestamp -> verify JWT -> derive verified userId/token hash ->
        BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY -> fresh now/JWT expiry recheck -> joined ACTIVE user/current-token projection
        -> own non-DELETED information -> map all ten keys/decrypt nullable fields -> COMMIT -> 200. Every SQL result
        returns to Application before branching or mapping.
    end note
app -> app: Generate requestId; validate UTC timestamp and empty query/body
note over app, infra
    No id/userId/query filters or body are accepted; reject non-empty query/body and invalid mandatory UTC
    timestamp with 400 E10001 before SQL. Generate requestId when omitted. No administrator role is required and
    no caller may choose another user's profile.
    Sensitive fields (emailAddress, firstName, lastName, phoneNumber, address) are decrypted server-side and
    returned as plain text over TLS. Preserve NULL without decrypting it. displayName/profilePicturePath are
    copied as stored; dateOfBirth is YYYY-MM-DD or null; gender is MALE/FEMALE/OTHER or null. Q20 is approved by
    the product owner on 2026-11-08: “คืน null สำหรับค่าว่างเดิม (แนะนำ)”. Project legacy empty gender to null
    with NULLIF(ui.gender, ''); preserve existing NULL and valid values. This is response normalization only: do
    not update stored history. New writes still accept MALE/FEMALE/OTHER or null under the upsert contract.
end note
alt Invalid timestamp or non-empty query/body
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
else Valid input
    app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub
    alt Missing or invalid JWT
        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
        api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
    else Verified JWT
        app -> app: userId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
        app -> infra: BEGIN REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
        note over app, infra
            Missing/malformed/invalid JWT gets generic 401 E10002 `Invalid or expired access token.` without SQL. Derive
            accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact presented JWT; never read target identity from the request or trust
            an unverified token. All SQL parameters are typed bound UUID/bytes/UTC timestamps, never interpolated input.
            The first SELECT joins the caller's ACTIVE m_user with its matching ACTIVE stored access token, checking
            exact hash, ownership and expiry > now, and projects only the six user-profile fields. A missing/inactive
            user or missing/revoked/expired/mismatched token returns the same 401 after ROLLBACK; do not query
            information or return partial data. Do not authorize from JWT validity alone or transaction-start NOW().
            No user/credential lock is taken for this inquiry. Credential/user validation is performed by the first
            joined read; role-assignment claims do not replace current credential checks and no live role query is
            needed for this self operation.
            All SQL is SELECT-only: do not create a missing information row, mark anything read, refresh tokens or
            update audit fields. COMMIT the read-only transaction only after mapping succeeds, then 200 S10000 `Inquiry
            User Profile Success`. On timeout before commit ROLLBACK then 408 E90001; on other unexpected failure
            ROLLBACK then generic 500 without bizCode. The endpoint adds no 403/404/409 and no pagination or write side
            effect.
        end note
        alt Read and mapping work completes
            app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now immediately before joined read; recheck JWT exp
            alt JWT still unexpired at fresh now
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get user
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Get user
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id,
                            u.email_address,
                            u.first_name,
                            u.last_name,
                            u.display_name,
                            u.profile_picture_path
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        JOIN authen.t_user_access_token at ON at.user_id = u.id
                        WHERE u.id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return six own-user fields gated by ACTIVE matching stored token/user, or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return six own-user fields gated by ACTIVE matching stored token/user, or no row
                alt Exactly one eligible user profile returned
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get information
                    infra -> m_user_information: QUERY - Get information
                    activate m_user_information
                        note right of m_user_information
                            SELECT
                                ui.phone_number,
                                ui.address,
                                ui.date_of_birth,
                                NULLIF(ui.gender, '') as gender
                            FROM authen.m_user_information ui
                            WHERE ui.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                            AND ui.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        end note
                        m_user_information -> infra: Return non-DELETED information with NULLIF gender, or no row
                    deactivate m_user_information
                    infra -> app: Return non-DELETED information with NULLIF gender, or no row
                    app -> app: data.userId = verified sub; data.emailAddress = decrypt stored email
                    app -> app: data.firstName/lastName = decrypt non-null stored values; data.displayName/profilePicturePath = stored values or null
                    alt Information row returned
                        app -> app: data.phoneNumber/address = decrypt non-null stored values; data.dateOfBirth = YYYY-MM-DD or null; data.gender = SQL normalized gender
                    else No non-DELETED information row
                        app -> app: data.phoneNumber/address/dateOfBirth/gender = null; do not create a row
                    end
                    app -> app: Emit exactly ten profile keys including explicit nulls; exclude username/password/token/hash/salt/session/audit/roles
                    app -> infra: COMMIT
                    infra -> app: Return completed consistent read-only profile
                    note over app, infra
                        Read the single row with the same userId and row_status <> DELETED, as enforced by
                        uq_m_user_information_user_id. Preserve the existing visibility of non-DELETED information, including
                        INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED; DELETED history is excluded. No information row is a normal state, not 404: return
                        null for phoneNumber/address/dateOfBirth/gender.
                        Return all ten data keys every time: userId, emailAddress, firstName, lastName, displayName,
                        profilePicturePath, phoneNumber, address, dateOfBirth, gender. A nullable value is explicit JSON null, never
                        an omitted key. data.userId is the verified caller id; emailAddress is mandatory and read only. Username and
                        the password are never returned, nor token/hash/salt, session, audit/lifecycle fields, role grants or
                        internal informationId. Unexpected mapping/decryption failure is generic 500, not partial 200.
                    end note
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry User Profile Success; all ten data keys
                    api -> page: Show own profile
                    page -> user: Display profile values
                else User or stored token missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
                end
            else JWT expired before the joined read
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
            end
        else Timeout before COMMIT
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
            api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
        else Unexpected SQL/decryption/mapping failure before COMMIT
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
            api -> page: Display failure; no partial profile
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
